{
  "comment": "Mc-incremental hand-set EMC values (#41, re-based in #47) for GT items ProjectE can't value: GT dusts, plates and blocks (dust = plate = ingot, block = 9 ingots), GT ingots with no ProjectE default metal value, parts, casings and steam-age machines, and GT fluid buckets (empty bucket + the fluid's value in kubejs/data/mcincremental_prestige/fluid_emc/fluids.json). Metal values derive from ProjectE's defaults (iron 256, copper 128, ...). Vanilla items and tags are not pinned, so ProjectE defaults apply, except a few that GT's recipe changes leave ProjectE unable to value (0 EMC): the empty and lava bucket and the iron, gold and copper blocks, pinned at ProjectE's own default values (bucket 3 iron = 768, lava bucket 832, block = 9 ingots). This file wins over ProjectE's datapack defaults.",
